Downstream changes
------------------

Four patches, one per fix, each against the pinned commit:

  0001  profile/download: accept the download parameters on an inherited
        descriptor. No upstream counterpart.
  0002  driver/at: accept a bare-decimal AT+CCHO response.
        Upstream: https://github.com/estkme-group/lpac/pull/449
  0003  driver/at: stop closing logical channels this process does not own.
        No upstream counterpart.
  0004  driver/at: bound every read with a deadline, and notice end of file.
        Upstream: https://github.com/estkme-group/lpac/pull/446
                  https://github.com/estkme-group/lpac/pull/448

The build enables the AT and stdio APDU backends and the stdio HTTP backend.
The curl HTTP backend and the uqmi APDU backend are not built.

This project's own files
------------------------

  /usr/libexec/apn-autoconfig-lpac/lpac-run
  /usr/share/apn-autoconfig-lpac/at-apdu-models

  Copyright the apn-autoconfig contributors, MIT.
  https://github.com/DarthAnwalt/openwrt-apn-autoconfig

  These are aggregated with the AGPL runtime, not derived from it: the launcher
  speaks to the LPA as a separate process, across the documented command line
  and the stdio bridge protocol, which is the same arm's-length relationship the
  official package's own /usr/bin/lpac wrapper has.
